  "final_response": "1. Run `git status` to see modified files under **“Changes not staged for commit.”** [recording-changes.004-stagin]  \n2. Stage a modified tracked file: `git add <filename>` – this moves the file into the staging area.  \n3. Run `git status` again to confirm the file now appears under **“Changes to be committed.”**  \n4. Create a commit that records the staged snapshot: `git commit -m \"commit message\"` .  \n   - As a shortcut for tracked files, you can combine staging and committing with `git commit -am \"commit message\"`.  \n5. For partial or selective staging, start interactive mode with `git add -i`.",
